<link rel="stylesheet" href="/s-18v2lq.css"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://nclexsim.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"The platform","item":"https://nclexsim.com/software"}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Vexcura platform?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Vexcura is one platform a nursing program runs on: an Epic-style academic EHR for charting practice, a full adaptive NCLEX-RN exam, clinical simulations, and instructor and compliance tools, with AI assistance labeled throughout. Schools license it; students and instructors use it free."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Vexcura a real electronic health record for patients?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Vexcura is an academic EHR for teaching. Its charts use made-up patients so students learn the workflow before clinicals; it is never used for real patient care."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is included in a Vexcura license?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every plan includes everything: the academic EHR, the adaptive exam and question bank, clinical simulations and megacodes, instructor tools, reporting, and the study guides. There are no student plans and no add-ons."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Vexcura replace ATI or HESI?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Vexcura works alongside them: students bring in their ATI, HESI, Kaplan, or UWorld scores and Vexcura builds study content around the gaps."}}]}</script></head><body><header class="top"><div class="w"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Vexcura home"><svg class="vxw" viewBox="-2 -86 472 96" aria-hidden="true"><style>@property --vxa{syntax:"<color>";inherits:true;initial-value:#4b4f86}@property --vxb{syntax:"<color>";inheri